<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2516" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andraemōn</span></b> ,
		ŏnis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀνδραίμων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The father of Amphissus and husband of Dryope</i>,
				<i>who was changed into a lotus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 9,
				333</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 363</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andraemōn</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Andrēmon</span></b> ,
				ŏnis, m., <i>father of Thoas</i>, <i>a combatant before
			Troy</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13, 357</span></i>; cf. Hom. Il. 2,
		638.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
